BFpp library -- std definition

	SYNOPSYS

{LOAD std/std.bfh}

	DEFINITION

std is a basic definitions set for bfpp library. 
it consist of two headers: stdop.bfh for "><[]+-.,", stdmacro.bfh for "[-]"

generally you shouldn't use std/std.bfh due to stdf/stdf.bfh

	MACROS

NEXT -- >
PREV -- <
INCR -- +
DECR -- -
CYCLE -- [
CYCL -- ]
READ -- ,
PRINT -- .
TONULL -- CYCLE DECR CYCL

	FUNCTIONS

see stdf/DEFINITION

	BFC BEHAVIOR

NEXT -- ptr += 1
PREV -- ptr -= 1
INCR -- tape[ptr] += 1
DECR -- tape[ptr] -= 1
CYCLE -- while(tape[ptr]) {
CYCL -- }
READ -- tape[ptr] = getchar()
PRINT -- putchar(tape[ptr])
TONULL -- tape[ptr] = 0
